::PC_U05_L02_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U05_L02_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.VC.2
Question:
Which statement correctly describes distance or midpoint on the complex plane?
{
~A. Use only the real parts.#This choice misses the two-part structure of complex numbers. Reconnect the real part to the horizontal coordinate and the imaginary part to the vertical coordinate.
=B. Use both real and imaginary coordinates.#Correct. A complex number a + bi is treated as the point (a, b), so both coordinates are needed.
~C. Use only the imaginary parts.#This choice misses the two-part structure of complex numbers. Reconnect the real part to the horizontal coordinate and the imaginary part to the vertical coordinate.
~D. Do not treat complex numbers as coordinate points.#This choice misses the two-part structure of complex numbers. Reconnect the real part to the horizontal coordinate and the imaginary part to the vertical coordinate.
}
